invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: the two seal calls take a packet in any version, so a Handshake
  packet goes out in a version the connection did not negotiate, which
  RFC 9369 section 4.1 forbids (rfc9369.txt:256-257).
  test/quic_version_tests.h seals at the Handshake level in four
  versions other than the negotiated one and requires CH_EINVAL with
  nothing written.

--- old
    if (level > CH_LEVEL_APPLICATION || !version_ok(q, level, version) ||
        (q->levels_ready & CH_QUIC_LEVEL_BIT(level, CH_KEY_WRITE)) == 0) {
--- new
    if (level > CH_LEVEL_APPLICATION ||
        (q->levels_ready & CH_QUIC_LEVEL_BIT(level, CH_KEY_WRITE)) == 0) {
